# Event pipeline Lua source

Use this as `main.lua` for the enabled `example-events` script. Its policy must allow `patchState` and `emitEvent`, with `manualTrigger` for both custom subscriptions. See [setup](dikciz://docs/recipes/event-setup).

```lua
function on_event(event)
  if event.type ~= "example.start" and event.type ~= "example.stop" then
    return { status = "Waiting" }
  end
  local running = event.type == "example.start"
  return {
    status = running and "Running" or "Stopped",
    actions = {
      { type = "patchState", values = { running = running } },
      {
        type = "emitEvent",
        event = "example.changed",
        payload = { running = running }
      }
    }
  }
end
```

The first action persists script state. The second publishes the result for rendered HTML subscribers. Inspect both action outcomes and the final script run status. This handler does not emit either input event, so it cannot loop back into its own subscriptions.

[HTML receiver](dikciz://docs/recipes/event-widget).

# Event pipeline HTML source

Put this in the widget's `html` field:

```html
<output id="event-status">Waiting</output>
```

Put this in its `javascript` field:

```javascript
const output = document.getElementById("event-status");
const acknowledge = values => selfWidget.patchState({
  ...selfWidget.state, ...values,
  ready: true, renderedText: output.textContent
});
function show(running) {
  output.textContent = running ? "Running" : "Stopped";
}
window.addEventListener("dikciz-ready", () => {
  if (typeof selfWidget.state.running === "boolean") {
    show(selfWidget.state.running);
  }
  dikciz.onEvent(async event => {
    if (event.type !== "example.changed") return;
    const running = event.payload.running === true;
    show(running);
    try {
      await acknowledge({ running });
    } catch (error) {
      console.error("Event acknowledgement failed", error.message);
    }
  });
  acknowledge({}).catch(error => {
    console.error("Readiness acknowledgement failed", error.message);
  });
});
```

Set `eventSubscriptions` in the saved widget record to `[{"event":"example.changed","minimumIntervalMilliseconds":0}]`. The field is not part of the typed `patchWidget` allowlist. Save the widget JSON or use the complete assembled configuration while preserving unrelated data.

Keep the page selected so the document remains rendered. The visible text changes when the event arrives. The saved `ready: true` confirms that the bridge is connected. `renderedText` is read from the output element after rendering. The state patch is a persisted acknowledgement that can be read remotely through `widgetGet` or `configGet`. After rendering is recreated, the saved Boolean restores the display.

[Setup and verification](dikciz://docs/recipes/event-setup). [Lua handler](dikciz://docs/recipes/event-lua).

## HTML widget JavaScript

A placed HTML widget receives `window.dikciz`, `selfWidget`, and `dikciz-ready` once its native message channel connects.

```javascript
window.addEventListener("dikciz-ready", async () => {
    const result = await dikciz.command("diagnostics");
    document.querySelector("#status").textContent = Object.keys(result).length;
});
```

`dikciz.request(document, options)` returns the complete command result/error envelope. `dikciz.command(type, fields, options)` returns its result or rejects with an error retaining `code`, `message`, `requestId`, `revision`, `permissionRequest` and the raw `response`. Both accept `options.responseTimeoutMilliseconds`; the default is at least 60 seconds or the operation timeout plus five seconds, and zero disables the response timer. A response timeout does not cancel dispatched work. `dikciz.dispatch({ actions })` uses the same typed action executor as Lua. `dikciz.fitContent()` asks the native frame to measure the current DOM.

`diagnostics` includes `htmlWidgetResources`: active renderer count, total UTF-8 bytes for generated documents on the selected page, and the configured per-page renderer and document-byte limits. These are launcher-owned resource inputs, not a claim about opaque Chromium process memory.

`selfWidget` and `dikciz.selfWidget` expose the current ID, page, full address, logical `cell`, state, and `get()`, `patch(values)`, and `patchState(values)` helpers. A widget document reports `cell`, never device pixels, so a widget author never persists a coordinate that rotation would invalidate. `dikciz.pages()` returns pages by ID, page address, and `home`. `await dikciz.home()` and `await dikciz.widget(address)` read current records after a configuration change.

Use `await dikciz.patchWidget(address, values)` for a full named-widget patch, or `await dikciz.patchWidgetState(address, values)` for its persisted state. Addresses are human-readable, for example `2H1V-weather-card`. A target on the current page receives `dikciz-state` without a document reload. A target on a different page is not treated as live DOM. Its saved state is available through `selfWidget.state` when that page is selected and its widget renders.

State patches keep the current document alive. Listen for `dikciz-state`:

```javascript
window.addEventListener("dikciz-state", event => {
    document.querySelector("#status").textContent = event.detail.status;
});
```

`dikciz.onEvent(listener)` receives matching native and custom events while the widget is rendered. It returns an unsubscribe function. The same document is sent as a `dikciz-event` window event. Select events in the widget's `eventSubscriptions` JSON field.

Publish a custom event with:

```javascript
await dikciz.emitEvent("weather.refresh.completed", { updatedAt: Date.now() });
```

Custom names are 1 through 128 characters, start with a letter, and use letters, digits, `.`, `_`, `:`, or `-`. Lua uses its matching `emitEvent` action.

The direct action vocabulary is `accessibilityAction`, `accessibilityGesture`, `accessibilityGlobalAction`, `selectPage`, `patchWidget`, `patchState`, `patchDom`, `launchApp`, `appAction`, `postNotification`, `sendSms`, `explicitIntent`, `emitEvent`, `mediaControl`, `setMediaVolume`, `notificationControl`, and `lockDevice`. `appAction` takes an `action` and a `component`. A script action has no selected page, so it rejects `addShortcut`. `sendSms` takes a dialable `recipient` and a `body`, and needs the `SEND_SMS` permission that `automationStatus` reports as `smsSend`. Android can save messages sent by non-default SMS apps into its SMS provider. This legacy typed action confirms submission only; use tracked `smsSend` and `smsStatus` for duplicate protection and sent/delivery evidence. `accessibilityAction` requires the current `snapshotId`, a `nodeId`, and one supported `action`; `setText` also requires `text`. Current policy and Android access decide whether an action can complete.

`patchDom` takes `widgetAddress`, a CSS `selector`, and a `values` object containing one or more of `text`, `html`, `value`, `className`, or `attributes`. It changes only a currently rendered HTML document and does not persist source or state. A target that is not rendered returns `target_not_rendered`.

For a complete event, Lua, HTML bridge, state, and action walkthrough, read the [scripting tutorial](scripting-tutorial.md).

`lockDevice` returns `device_admin_inactive` when Android Device Administration is not active. It does not open Android Settings. Open **Settings**, then **Automation**, then **Set up full device access** to request that access.

The native bridge holds at most 32 waiting requests and accepts at most one MiB of UTF-8 JSON per request. The supplied JavaScript API separately allows at most 32 outstanding promises, so ordinary `dikciz.command()` calls are backpressured before native saturation. Raw channel users can still receive `busy` when the native queue is full. Every rejected HTML command is logged as `web_command_rejected` with the HTML widget ID, HTML kind, and error reason, and is available through both log transports. A state patch does not reload the WebView. Replacing HTML, CSS, JavaScript, or the whole configuration can destroy the calling document. Lifecycle commands acknowledge their response after promise handlers run, before destroying that document.

## Handle an event

```javascript
function onEvent(event) {
    const count = (context.state.count || 0) + 1;
    return {
        status: "Counter updated",
        actions: [
            {type: "patchState", values: {count: count}},
            {type: "emitEvent", event: "example.counter.updated", payload: {count: count}}
        ]
    };
}
```

This handler needs an enabled policy allowing `manualTrigger` and actions `patchState` and `emitEvent`, plus an enabled subscription. Use `event: "manual"` for `automationTrigger`, or the exact custom event name for another component's input. Do not add a separate `customEventName` field to subscription files. Read the [policy and subscription schema](dikciz-configuration.md#lua-scripts-and-automation) and [event pipeline](scripting-tutorial.md#build-a-complete-custom-event-workflow).

`event` contains `type`, `source`, `timestampMilliseconds`, `coalescingKey`, `payload` and local `time.hour24`/`time.minute`. `context` contains `scriptId`, `state`, `widgets`, `androidAccess` and optional `accessibility`. Input objects are read-only. Return typed actions to persist changes; `patchState` merges fields into this script's state and preserves explicit JSON nulls and array positions. A null value clears the saved value while retaining its key. Globals are fresh for each invocation. Lua uses `on_event`; JavaScript uses `onEvent`. The returned action schema is shared.

## dikciz_accessibility_snapshot

Read a bounded snapshot of the active Android accessibility tree. The owner must first enable Dikciz cross-app automation in Android Accessibility settings.

Ordinary command: `accessibilitySnapshot`. [Token scope definitions](token-permissions.md#accessibilitysnapshot). [Result envelope and task guides](developer-manual.md#result-contract).

WebView invocation: `await dikciz.command("accessibilitySnapshot", fields)`. Headless JavaScript: `context.request(Object.assign({}, fields, {type: "accessibilitySnapshot"}))`. Lua: set `request.type = "accessibilitySnapshot"`, then call `context.request(request)`. `fields`/`request` must contain the required parameters below. WebView `command` unwraps `result`; backend requests return the complete response envelope. [JavaScript methods](javascript-api.md) and [Lua types and errors](lua-api.md).

| Parameter | Required | Type | Default | Definition and bounds |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `autoRequestPermissions` | No | `boolean` | `false` | Show owner permission recovery when required. Defaults to false; explicit permission-request tools always ask. Never grants access or retries an operation. |



```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "autoRequestPermissions": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "description": "Show owner permission recovery when required. Defaults to false; explicit permission-request tools always ask. Never grants access or retries an operation.",
      "default": false
    }
  },
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

## dikciz_activity_cancel

Request best-effort thread interruption of one running activity. Does not roll back completed effects or prove Android stopped work. Poll activityRead. Requires the matching explicit operation grant for scoped remote clients.

Ordinary command: `activityCancel`. [Token scope definitions](token-permissions.md#activitycancel). [Result envelope and task guides](developer-manual.md#result-contract).

WebView invocation: `await dikciz.command("activityCancel", fields)`. Headless JavaScript: `context.request(Object.assign({}, fields, {type: "activityCancel"}))`. Lua: set `request.type = "activityCancel"`, then call `context.request(request)`. `fields`/`request` must contain the required parameters below. WebView `command` unwraps `result`; backend requests return the complete response envelope. [JavaScript methods](javascript-api.md) and [Lua types and errors](lua-api.md).

| Parameter | Required | Type | Default | Definition and bounds |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `activityId` | Yes | `string` | `Not declared` | See the complete schema below. {"maxLength": 36} |
| `autoRequestPermissions` | No | `boolean` | `false` | Ask the owner to grant missing Android access. Never grants access or retries automatically. |



```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "activityId": {
      "type": "string",
      "maxLength": 36
    },
    "autoRequestPermissions": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": false,
      "description": "Ask the owner to grant missing Android access. Never grants access or retries automatically."
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "activityId"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

## dikciz_activity_read

Read persistent command metadata without arguments or payloads. Requires the matching explicit operation grant for scoped remote clients. Includes actor, request ID, duration and completed/rejected/failed/interrupted/running state. Interrupted outcomes may be unknown. Seven-day retention and bounded pagination.

Ordinary command: `activityRead`. [Token scope definitions](token-permissions.md#activityread). [Result envelope and task guides](developer-manual.md#result-contract).

WebView invocation: `await dikciz.command("activityRead", fields)`. Headless JavaScript: `context.request(Object.assign({}, fields, {type: "activityRead"}))`. Lua: set `request.type = "activityRead"`, then call `context.request(request)`. `fields`/`request` must contain the required parameters below. WebView `command` unwraps `result`; backend requests return the complete response envelope. [JavaScript methods](javascript-api.md) and [Lua types and errors](lua-api.md).

| Parameter | Required | Type | Default | Definition and bounds |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `actor` | No | `string` | `Not declared` | See the complete schema below. {"maxLength": 80} |
| `autoRequestPermissions` | No | `boolean` | `false` | Ask the owner to grant missing Android access. Never grants access or retries automatically. |
| `limit` | No | `integer` | `Not declared` | See the complete schema below. {"minimum": 1, "maximum": 200} |
| `mutatingOnly` | No | `boolean` | `false` | See the complete schema below. |
| `offset` | No | `integer` | `Not declared` | See the complete schema below. {"minimum": 0, "maximum": 1000000} |
| `outcome` | No | `string` | `Not declared` | See the complete schema below. {"maxLength": 32} |



```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "limit": {
      "type": "integer",
      "minimum": 1,
      "maximum": 200
    },
    "offset": {
      "type": "integer",
      "minimum": 0,
      "maximum": 1000000
    },
    "actor": {
      "type": "string",
      "maxLength": 80
    },
    "outcome": {
      "type": "string",
      "maxLength": 32
    },
    "mutatingOnly": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": false
    },
    "autoRequestPermissions": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": false,
      "description": "Ask the owner to grant missing Android access. Never grants access or retries automatically."
    }
  },
  "required": [],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

## dikciz_add_widget

Place one new top-level item in the first fitting free cells of the selected page grid. Rejects with page_full and writes nothing when no space fits. Use dikciz_widget_move and dikciz_widget_resize to place it afterwards.

Ordinary command: `addWidget`. [Token scope definitions](token-permissions.md#addwidget). [Result envelope and task guides](developer-manual.md#result-contract).

WebView invocation: `await dikciz.command("addWidget", fields)`. Headless JavaScript: `context.request(Object.assign({}, fields, {type: "addWidget"}))`. Lua: set `request.type = "addWidget"`, then call `context.request(request)`. `fields`/`request` must contain the required parameters below. WebView `command` unwraps `result`; backend requests return the complete response envelope. [JavaScript methods](javascript-api.md) and [Lua types and errors](lua-api.md).

| Parameter | Required | Type | Default | Definition and bounds |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `autoRequestPermissions` | No | `boolean` | `false` | Show owner permission recovery when required. Defaults to false; explicit permission-request tools always ask. Never grants access or retries an operation. |
| `widgetType` | Yes | `string` | `Not declared` | Item type to create: html, appGroup, or scriptDashboard. {"maximum": 256} |



```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "widgetType": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Item type to create: html, appGroup, or scriptDashboard.",
      "maximum": 256
    },
    "autoRequestPermissions": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "description": "Show owner permission recovery when required. Defaults to false; explicit permission-request tools always ask. Never grants access or retries an operation.",
      "default": false
    }
  },
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "required": [
    "widgetType"
  ]
}
```

## dikciz_android_api_callback

Create a public SDK interface callback that records typed invocations for androidApiObjects. returns maps exact callback overload ids to constant return values; unspecified non-void callbacks are rejected. No scripts run on Binder threads. Register with a writable SDK call and unregister before releasing. Public non-final SDK callback classes use a generated subclass. Constructor defaults to new(); select an exact SDK constructor when arguments are needed.

Ordinary command: `androidApiCallback`. [Token scope definitions](token-permissions.md#androidapicallback). [Result envelope and task guides](developer-manual.md#result-contract).

WebView invocation: `await dikciz.command("androidApiCallback", fields)`. Headless JavaScript: `context.request(Object.assign({}, fields, {type: "androidApiCallback"}))`. Lua: set `request.type = "androidApiCallback"`, then call `context.request(request)`. `fields`/`request` must contain the required parameters below. WebView `command` unwraps `result`; backend requests return the complete response envelope. [JavaScript methods](javascript-api.md) and [Lua types and errors](lua-api.md).

| Parameter | Required | Type | Default | Definition and bounds |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `arguments` | No | `array` | `Not declared` | Required ordered arguments, including explicit nulls. Use {objectRef:ID}, {className:SDK_CLASS}, {bytesBase64:BASE64}, {long:DECIMAL} or {arrayType:SDK_TYPE,values:[...]}. No inferred overloads or nested calls. {"maxItems": 64} |
| `autoRequestPermissions` | No | `boolean` | `false` | Ask the owner to grant missing Android access. Never grants access or retries automatically. |
| `className` | Yes | `string` | `Not declared` | Exact public className from androidApiDiscover. {"maxLength": 256} |
| `constructor` | No | `string` | `Not declared` | Exact SDK constructor id, defaults to new(). {"maxLength": 2048} |
| `returns` | No | `object` | `Not declared` | See the complete schema below. |



```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "className": {
      "type": "string",
      "maxLength": 256,
      "description": "Exact public className from androidApiDiscover."
    },
    "returns": {
      "type": "object"
    },
    "constructor": {
      "type": "string",
      "maxLength": 2048,
      "description": "Exact SDK constructor id, defaults to new()."
    },
    "arguments": {
      "type": "array",
      "maxItems": 64,
      "items": {},
      "description": "Required ordered arguments, including explicit nulls. Use {objectRef:ID}, {className:SDK_CLASS}, {bytesBase64:BASE64}, {long:DECIMAL} or {arrayType:SDK_TYPE,values:[...]}. No inferred overloads or nested calls."
    },
    "autoRequestPermissions": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": false,
      "description": "Ask the owner to grant missing Android access. Never grants access or retries automatically."
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "className"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

## dikciz_android_api_invoke

Invoke a public SDK method, constructor or field read/set with writable access. Select an exact discovered member. Set a mutable field with set:NAME and one argument. Android permissions, roles, hardware and foreground restrictions still apply. Raw filesystem, private app storage, reflection and dynamic code APIs are excluded; use the dedicated protected file/shell APIs. Wrap long operations in jobStart. No automatic replay after process death.

Ordinary command: `androidApiInvoke`. [Token scope definitions](token-permissions.md#androidapiinvoke). [Result envelope and task guides](developer-manual.md#result-contract).

WebView invocation: `await dikciz.command("androidApiInvoke", fields)`. Headless JavaScript: `context.request(Object.assign({}, fields, {type: "androidApiInvoke"}))`. Lua: set `request.type = "androidApiInvoke"`, then call `context.request(request)`. `fields`/`request` must contain the required parameters below. WebView `command` unwraps `result`; backend requests return the complete response envelope. [JavaScript methods](javascript-api.md) and [Lua types and errors](lua-api.md).

| Parameter | Required | Type | Default | Definition and bounds |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `arguments` | Yes | `array` | `Not declared` | Required ordered arguments, including explicit nulls. Use {objectRef:ID}, {className:SDK_CLASS}, {bytesBase64:BASE64}, {long:DECIMAL} or {arrayType:SDK_TYPE,values:[...]}. No inferred overloads or nested calls. {"maxItems": 64} |
| `autoRequestPermissions` | No | `boolean` | `false` | Ask the owner to grant missing Android access. Never grants access or retries automatically. |
| `className` | Yes | `string` | `Not declared` | Exact public className from androidApiDiscover. {"maxLength": 256} |
| `idempotencyKey` | Yes | `string` | `Not declared` | Unique process-scoped key. Same payload returns its original result; changed payload fails. For durable submission use jobStart. {"maxLength": 80} |
| `member` | Yes | `string` | `Not declared` | Exact discovered overload id, including parameter types. Constructors use new(...); fields use field:NAME. {"maxLength": 2048} |
| `target` | No | `string` | `Not declared` | Omit for constructors and static members. Otherwise context, activity, service:NAME or an objectRef from a previous result. {"maxLength": 256} |
| `thread` | No | `string` | `Not declared` | auto, main or background. Auto follows SDK MainThread/UiThread annotations. {"maxLength": 16} |
| `timeoutMilliseconds` | No | `integer` | `30000` | See the complete schema below. {"minimum": 1, "maximum": 300000} |



```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "className": {
      "type": "string",
      "maxLength": 256,
      "description": "Exact public className from androidApiDiscover."
    },
    "member": {
      "type": "string",
      "maxLength": 2048,
      "description": "Exact discovered overload id, including parameter types. Constructors use new(...); fields use field:NAME."
    },
    "timeoutMilliseconds": {
      "type": "integer",
      "minimum": 1,
      "maximum": 300000,
      "default": 30000
    },
    "thread": {
      "type": "string",
      "maxLength": 16,
      "description": "auto, main or background. Auto follows SDK MainThread/UiThread annotations."
    },
    "target": {
      "type": "string",
      "maxLength": 256,
      "description": "Omit for constructors and static members. Otherwise context, activity, service:NAME or an objectRef from a previous result."
    },
    "arguments": {
      "type": "array",
      "maxItems": 64,
      "items": {},
      "description": "Required ordered arguments, including explicit nulls. Use {objectRef:ID}, {className:SDK_CLASS}, {bytesBase64:BASE64}, {long:DECIMAL} or {arrayType:SDK_TYPE,values:[...]}. No inferred overloads or nested calls."
    },
    "idempotencyKey": {
      "type": "string",
      "maxLength": 80,
      "description": "Unique process-scoped key. Same payload returns its original result; changed payload fails. For durable submission use jobStart."
    },
    "autoRequestPermissions": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": false,
      "description": "Ask the owner to grant missing Android access. Never grants access or retries automatically."
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "className",
    "member",
    "arguments",
    "idempotencyKey"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
